\paragraph{Sparsity cliff at 30\%.}
\label{sec:sparsity_cliff}
All tested methods collapse at 30\% sparsity (Table~\ref{tab:sparsity_cliff}, Appendix~\ref{sec:appendix_sparsity_cliff}), validating 20\% as the operating point.

\paragraph{Inference efficiency.}
\label{sec:inference}
Pruning reduces parameters by 19\% (7.62B$\to$6.16B) and memory by ${\sim}$28\%, with TTFT improving 18\%; per-token throughput decreases 19\% due to non-uniform layer widths (Appendix~\ref{sec:appendix_inference}).

\paragraph{CKA coefficient $\alpha$ ablation.}
\label{sec:ablation}
Post-prune accuracy across $\alpha \in \{0.0, 0.25, 0.5, 1.0, 2.0, 4.0\}$ shows a non-monotonic pattern: intermediate values create suboptimal trade-offs where importance and redundancy signals partially cancel (Appendix~\ref{sec:appendix_alpha}).

